ed to charter a floating storage and regasification unit from Mitsui O.S.K. Lines", "SEPT 19:The date when Japan's Mitsui O.S.K. Lines, Norway's Yara, and Singapore's Global Centre for Maritime Decarbonisation completed an ammonia cargo transfer operation in Australia", "SINGAPORE:", "WILLIAM CLARK:William Clark is the contact person and Sales Director for Tesla, Inc. in the procurement agreement", "\"K\" LINE:\"K\" LINE, also known as Kawasaki Kisen Kaisha, Ltd., is a logistics company rooted in the shipping industry, operating a diverse fleet of more than 400 vessels worldwide. Established in 1919, it provides reliable maritime transport services and focuses on digital transformation, environmental technologies, and safety/ship quality management to offer safe and optimized services that prioritize the customer.\"", "INMARSAT MARITIME:Inmarsat Maritime, a Viasat company, powers the digitalization of the maritime industry with over 40 years of experience. It offers reliable and innovative solutions that enable ship owners and operators to stay connected, navigate safely, enhance operational efficiency, and ensure crew welfare. Inmarsat Maritime is based in Viasat’s global international business headquarters in London, United Kingdom.", "VIASAT:Viasat is a global communications company that believes everyone and everything in the world can be connected. With offices in 24 countries, Viasat is developing a global communications network to provide high-quality, reliable, secure, affordable, and fast connections. In May 2023, Viasat completed its acquisition of Inmarsat, combining the teams, technologies, and resources of the two companies to create a new global communications partner.", "NEXUSWAVE:NexusWave is a new bonded network service launched by Inmarsat Maritime in May 2023. It integrates multiple high-speed networks in real time to enable high-speed, always-on ship-to-shore communications. NexusWave offers high-speed connectivity, unlimited data, global coverage, and secure infrastructure for office-like and home-like experiences. It integrates Global Xpress (GX) Ka-band, low-Earth orbit (LEO) services, and coastal LTE service, enhanced by an L-band layer for resiliency.", "AKIHIRO FUJIMARU:Akihiro Fujimaru is the Managing Executive Officer of \"K\" LINE. He has emphasized the importance of fast, reliable, and global connectivity services for enhancing safety, quality, and the well-being of the crew, as well as supporting digitalization initiatives and automated ship navigation.", "BEN PALMER:Ben Palmer OBE is the President of Inmarsat Maritime. He has expressed honor in partnering with \"K\" LINE to trial NexusWave on its fleet, highlighting the strategic foresight of \"K\" LINE’s commitment to leveraging advanced technology for operational success and competitive edge.", "YUKIKAZU MYOCHIN:Yukikazu Myochin is the President & CEO of \"K\" LINE. He is involved in the partnership with Inmarsat Maritime for the trial of NexusWave on \"K\" LINE's fleet."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}